//# OPTIONS --keep-unused

abstract xor TrafficLight_1
	initial xor on -->> off
		initial xor normal  // no -->> flashing because we don't want to force it, it's optional
			initial green --> yellow
			yellow --> red
			red --> green
		xor flashing -->> normal
			initial yellow_on --> yellow_off
			yellow_off --> yellow_on
	off --> on

// The scenarios are in tmp_TrafficLight1_*.cfr, which import this model.

/*
Construct	            | Meaning
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
on -->> off	            | on lasts any number of steps but must eventually become off.
off --> on	            | off lasts exactly one step.
initial xor normal	    | Every time on starts, it starts in normal, and initial green makes it start in green.
                        | Re-entering on starts it again.
no transition on normal	| normal may stay or switch to flashing at any step.
flashing -->> normal	| flashing lasts at least one step and must eventually end.
green --> yellow etc.	| The strict cycles inside a state.
 */


 /* Traces found for all 5 scenarios:
- a long on,
- normal -> flashing -> normal,
- flashing -> off,
- never flashing, and
- a long flashing.

No counterexample to the spec:
- on always ends,
- off lasts one step,
- every on starts in normal/green,
- flashing ends in normal or off,
- and the green -> yellow cycle holds.
*/